.TH CENTCOM-INSTALL-HANDLER 1 "" "centcom 0.1.0 (contract 1.2.0)" "Centcom"
.SH NAME
centcom\-install\-handler \- make centcom:// links open with Centcom
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B centcom install\-handler [\-\-uninstall] [\-\-dry\-run]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Registers Centcom as the handler for centcom:// links in your own account (no sudo): a desktop entry on Linux, an app in ~/Applications on macOS, a registry entry under HKCU on Windows. \-\-dry\-run only lists what it would do; \-\-uninstall removes what it made.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-uninstall
remove the handler this command made
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
list what would be done and change nothing
.SH SEE ALSO
centcom help, https://centcom.dev/docs
